president.

00:10:26.358 --> 00:10:28.494
I think this -- that we're
too close to the election.

00:10:28.494 --> 00:10:30.329
The president, who is elected
in November,

00:10:30.329 --> 00:10:31.964
should be the one who
makes this decision.

00:10:31.964 --> 00:10:34.967
-The Senate will approx--
appropriately revisit the matter

00:10:34.967 --> 00:10:38.771
after the American people finish
making in November the decision

00:10:38.771 --> 00:10:41.173
they've already started
making today.

00:10:41.173 --> 00:10:43.709
The American people are
perfectly capable

00:10:43.709 --> 00:10:46.244
of having their say,

00:10:46.244 --> 00:10:50.349
their say, on this issue.

00:10:50.349 --> 00:10:53.585
So let's give them a voice.

00:10:53.585 --> 00:10:56.087
Let's let the American people
decide.

00:10:56.087 --> 00:11:00.359
-It has been 80 years since
a Supreme Court vacancy

00:11:00.359 --> 00:11:02.528
was nominated and confirmed
in an election year.

00:11:02.528 --> 00:11:04.896
There is a long tradition
that you don't do this

00:11:04.896 --> 00:11:05.764
in an election year.

00:11:05.764 --> 00:11:07.800
This should be a decision

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:09.034
for the people, George.

00:11:09.034 --> 00:11:10.435
Let the election decide.

00:11:10.435 --> 00:11:12.437
-I don't think we should be
moving forward on a nominee

00:11:12.437 --> 00:11:14.206
in the last year of this
president's term.

00:11:14.206 --> 00:11:16.008
I would say that if it was
a Republican president.

00:11:16.008 --> 00:11:17.309
-The American people
need a chance

00:11:17.309 --> 00:11:20.045
to weigh in on this issue
on who will fill that seat.

00:11:20.045 --> 00:11:21.713
They will have that chance
this November,

00:11:21.713 --> 00:11:23.048
and they ought to have
that chance.

00:11:23.048 --> 00:11:24.884
-This is about principle.

00:11:24.884 --> 00:11:28.320
Not the person the president
has nominated.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:32.024
And it's why the majority
of the Senate has chosen to use

00:11:32.024 --> 00:11:34.693
this unique situation
as an opportunity

00:11:34.693 --> 00:11:36.995
to let the American people
have a voice.

00:11:36.995 --> 00:11:39.098
-I want you to use my words
against me

00:11:39.098 --> 00:11:41.866
if there's a Republican
President in 2016

00:11:41.866 --> 00:11:45.271
and a vacancy occurs in the last
year of the first term.

00:11:45.271 --> 00:11:47.339
You can say Lindsey Graham said,

00:11:47.339 --> 00:11:50.675
"Let's let the next President.
whoever it might be,

00:11:50.675 --> 00:11:52.277
make that nomination."

00:11:52.277 --> 00:11:56.948
If an opening comes
in the last year

00:11:56.948 --> 00:11:59.251
of President Trump's term,

00:11:59.251 --> 00:12:02.788
And the primary process
is started,

00:12:02.788 --> 00:12:04.456
We'll wait to the next election.

00:12:04.456 --> 00:12:07.759
And I've got a pretty good
chance of being the judic--

00:12:07.759 --> 00:12:09.194
-You're on the record.
-Yeah.

00:12:09.194 --> 00:12:11.496
-All right.
-Hold the tape.

00:12:11.496 --> 00:12:12.764
-Holy [bleep]

00:12:12.764 --> 00:12:15.067
[ Chuckles ]
Just in time for fall.

00:12:15.067 --> 00:12:17.136
Jesus!
That montage was so long,

00:12:17.136 --> 00:12:19.171
my hair grew out again
and again.

00:12:19.171 --> 00:12:21.640
I get that the hypocrisy
is baked in.

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:23.409
Pointing it out won't change
their minds.

00:12:23.409 --> 00:12:24.977
It's like telling
a middle school bully,

00:12:24.977 --> 00:12:27.079
"Giving me a wedgie
won't make your parents

00:12:27.079 --> 00:12:28.714
get back together."
He knows that.

00:12:28.714 --> 00:12:31.116
He just wants to give you
that wedgie.

00:12:31.116 --> 00:12:33.486
Still, it's worth documenting
just how obvious

00:12:33.486 --> 00:12:34.953
and degrading the lies were.

00:12:34.953 --> 00:12:37.889
And remembering this the next
time they pretend to care

00:12:37.889 --> 00:12:40.625
about some obvious [bleep] like
cutting the deficit

00:12:40.625 --> 00:12:42.394
or respecting the courts.

00:12:42.394 --> 00:12:47.198
Also, it's striking just how
specific their promises were.

00:12:47.198 --> 00:12:48.834
"This is about principle.

00:12:48.834 --> 00:12:51.236
I'd say that if a Republican was
president.

00:12:51.236 --> 00:12:52.604
Use my words against me."

00:12:52.604 --> 00:12:54.806
I'm shocked Lindsey Graham
doesn't get up there

00:12:54.806 --> 00:12:56.175
and say [As Graham]
Mark my words.

00:12:56.175 --> 00:12:59.578
If 45 days before the 2020
presidential election,

00:12:59.578 --> 00:13:02.781
An iconic liberal justice
passes away and requests

00:13:02.781 --> 00:13:04.949
as her dying wish that she not
be replaced

00:13:04.949 --> 00:13:06.351
until after the election,

00:13:06.351 --> 00:13:09.755
which is taking place during
a once-in-a-century pandemic

00:13:09.755 --> 00:13:11.990
Just two weeks after it's
announced that

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:14.025
"Keeping Up With
the Kardashians" is ending,

00:13:14.025 --> 00:13:15.661
then you could use my words
against me.

00:13:15.661 --> 00:13:18.063
I promise I will not vote
on a justice nominated

00:13:18.063 --> 00:13:19.965
by president --
-Donald Prump.

00:13:19.965 --> 00:13:23.268
-Seriously, though, when you
watch a montage like that

00:13:23.268 --> 00:13:26.138
and then see all the same people
scurrying

00:13:26.138 --> 00:13:28.374
as quickly as possible
to reverse themselves

00:13:28.374 --> 00:13:32.044
four years later, it's almost
like the lying and the hypocrisy

00:13:32.044 --> 00:13:33.578
are the point.

00:13:33.578 --> 00:13:36.815
Like, they are trying to rub our
noses in just how shameless

00:13:36.815 --> 00:13:39.351
and unaccountable they are that
they don't care about democracy,

00:13:39.351 --> 00:13:41.219
that they can do whatever
they want.

00:13:41.219 --> 00:13:44.923
For example, when Ted Cruz was
asked about comments from 2016,

00:13:44.923 --> 00:13:46.591
he dismissed them as
meaningless.

00:13:46.591 --> 00:13:50.629
-Look. We had this fight at the
end of the Barack Obama term.

00:13:50.629 --> 00:13:53.465
And at the time, all the
Democrats were saying

00:13:53.465 --> 00:13:55.301
"Confirm the nominee.
Confirm the nominee."

00:13:55.301 --> 00:13:56.468
And all the Republicans were
saying,

00:13:56.468 --> 00:13:57.769
"We're not going to confirm
the nominee."

00:13:57.769 --> 00:13:59.572
And so, we've got a situation.

00:13:59.572 --> 00:14:01.674
You just played a quote from me
in 2016.

00:14:01.674 --> 00:14:03.842
We can play that game
all day long.

00:14:03.842 --> 00:14:06.345
-[ As Cruz ] If you want to play
clips of me lying through

00:14:06.345 --> 00:14:08.514
my weird, little teeth,
while condescending

00:14:08.514 --> 00:14:10.516
like a French waiter
at Disney Land,

00:14:10.516 --> 00:14:12.284
we can play that game
all day long.

00:14:12.284 --> 00:14:14.153
[ Normal voice ] Democrats
have to internalize the fact

00:14:14.153 --> 00:14:16.121
that this is not about
principle.

00:14:16.121 --> 00:14:18.189
This is about raw,
political power.

00:14:18.189 --> 00:14:21.793
And they need to use every tool
at their disposal to stop it.

00:14:21.793 --> 00:14:24.196
The Senate majority
that won fewer votes

00:14:24.196 --> 00:14:27.499
than the Senate minority
wants to help a corrupt autocrat

00:14:27.499 --> 00:14:29.835
install an unprecedented
conservative super majority

00:14:29.835 --> 00:14:32.704
on the Supreme Court, appointed
largely by presidents

00:14:32.704 --> 00:14:34.806
who lost the popular vote,
including, of course,

00:14:34.806 --> 00:14:36.741
the current president...
-Donald Prump.

00:14:36.741 --> 00:14:38.610
-This has been "A Closer Look."

